### Jedrock ###
# The runnable server, built into the project root by `mvn package` so it lands beside the folders a
# run actually uses (target/ is excluded in the IDE, so a jar in there is a jar you never see).
/jedrock.jar
# Runtime config written on first run (the templates live in jedrock-core resources).
/jedrock.properties
/pipeline.yml
# Saved world data, written at runtime. The default world is generated on first run and never committed;
# what a run writes on top of any other world (scenes, regions, a half-written save) isn't either.
/worlds/world/
/worlds/*/level.jdw.tmp
/worlds/*/scenes.jdb
/worlds/*/regions.jdb
# The log folder, and the server's own bookkeeping (ops, permissions, remembered worlds, script storage).
/logs/
/data/
# The pre-layout locations of the same files, in a working copy that hasn't been migrated yet.
/world/
/ops.txt
/permissions.txt
/player-worlds.txt
/plugin-storage.jdb
/plugin-storage.jdb.tmp
